course: dictionary
lesson: 8533
title: Sweet or savoury?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Savoury is a word about taste. Savoury food is salty or spicy, not sweet. Cheese, crisps, pies and soup are savoury. When you meet a food word, ask yourself: is it sweet? If not, it may be savoury.
explain: Look at the words around it. «A savoury pie» and «sweet or savoury?» show that savoury is the opposite of sweet. Food lessons often sort dishes into two groups: sweet and savoury.
explain: In the UK, a savoury can also be a small salty snack, so it can be a noun too. Americans spell it savory. «Not very savoury» is different: it describes someone or something that is not nice or respectable, so check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Savoury means salty or spicy, not sweet.
fact: The tongue can sense five basic tastes: sweet, salty, sour, bitter and savoury.
fact: Savoury taste is also called umami, and it is found in cheese and tomatoes.
fact: «Not very savoury» means not nice or respectable.
fact: In the UK, a savoury is a small salty snack, and the plural is savouries.
exercise: Which food is savoury? | *A cheese and tomato pizza | A jam doughnut | A chocolate sponge cake | A bowl of fruit salad
exercise: «Not very savoury» describes what? | *Someone or something not nice or respectable | A bright blue sky | Something very salty and spicy | A sweet cake
exercise: Ella says savoury means sour. What is the right answer? | Bitter, like a warning poison | *Salty or spicy, not sweet | Sweet, like sugar | Sour, like a lemon
test: The savoury taste is also called what? | *Umami | Sugary | Minty | Crunchy
test: What is the opposite of savoury? | Bitter | *Sweet | Salty | Spicy
exam: In a shop, a sign says «a savoury for your lunch». What is a savoury here? | A large bowl of fruit | A sweet cake | *A small salty snack | A type of bitter tea
